pre_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
NOTE: mpv-dovi-vfx-git carries four extra filters that are dlopen()-based,
      not linked into the binary:

        hwup     upload CUDA/NVDEC frames to a CUDA device buffer
        vsr      NVIDIA NGX VideoSuperRes (AI upscale)
        truehdr  NVIDIA NGX TrueHDR (SDR -> HDR10)
        vfg      NVIDIA VideoFrameGeneration (frame interpolation)

      They need the NVIDIA VFX SDK runtime. The loader looks for it in
      $HOME/.local/lib/vsr-player and enables the filters when it is present;
      when it is missing, mpv still runs normally and the filters just error
      out on first use.

      Required runtime pieces, none of which are hard package dependencies:
        - the proprietary NVIDIA driver (libcuda.so.1)
        - the 'cuda' package (libnvrtc.so.13, used to JIT the YUV->RGBA kernel)
        - an RTX GPU with the NGX models for VSR / TrueHDR / VFG

      The AI chain must decode through NVDEC (--hwdec=nvdec). With
      --hwdec=vulkan the frames cannot be uploaded to CUDA and hwup disables
      the whole chain.

      The Dolby Vision P7 FEL path is unaffected and needs no extra runtime.
EOF
}

pre_upgrade() {
  if pacman -Q mpv-dovi-git >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    cat <<'EOF'
NOTE: this package replaces mpv-dovi-git. It is the same mpv commit
      (488fec0789) with the same static libplacebo/FFmpeg DoVi stack, plus the
      NVIDIA VFX filters. Your ~/.config/mpv/mpv.conf keeps working unchanged.
EOF
  fi
}
